<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Diperdana requests suspension.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Diperdana requests suspension.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian shipping company Diperdana Corporation Bhd, through its merchant bankers, asked the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange to suspend trading in its shares beginning November 1.</p>
<p>In a statement issued by the company on Thursday, Diperdana said the suspension was being requested due to discussions currently taking place &quot;for a possible acquisition of a substantial stake in a listed company&quot;.</p>
<p>No further details were given in the statement and company officials could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>Shipping stocks have moved up this year on anticipation of a consolidation within the industry. The government has urged mergers because freight costs have been a major contributor to the country's balance of payment deficit.</p>
<p>Diperdana closed unchanged at 20.80 ringgit on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
